Redox has getauxval but does not define Linux's AT_SECURE auxiliary-vector key.
Use OCaml's existing issetugid/UID/GID fallback when that key is absent, rather
than assigning a Linux auxiliary-vector constant to another operating system.

--- a/otherlibs/unix/envir_unix.c
+++ b/otherlibs/unix/envir_unix.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
 
 static char **secure_environ(void)
 {
-#ifdef HAS_GETAUXVAL
+#if defined(HAS_GETAUXVAL) && defined(AT_SECURE)
   if (!getauxval(AT_SECURE))
     return environ;
   else
